Hi guys,

I am trying to implement a test in the class `ProjectTasksTestCase` but I am getting a `NullPointerException` in the statement `MatcherAssert.assertThat(tasks.ofContract(contractId)`. Do you have any idea why is it happening? Is there something wrong with the mock of `task`?

```
    /**
     * Should return tasks for contract.
     */
    @Test
    public void returnTasksForContract() {
        final Contract.Id contractId = new Contract.Id("foo", "mihai",
                Provider.Names.GITHUB, Roles.DEV);

        final Contributor mihai = Mockito.mock(Contributor.class);
        Mockito.when(mihai.username()).thenReturn("mihai");
        Mockito.when(mihai.provider()).thenReturn(Provider.Names.GITHUB);
        final Task task = Mockito.mock(Task.class);
        Mockito.when(task.assignee()).thenReturn(mihai);
        Mockito.when(task.role()).thenReturn(Roles.DEV);

        final Storage storage = Mockito.mock(Storage.class);

        final Tasks tasks = new ProjectTasks(
                "foo", Provider.Names.GITHUB,
                List.of(
                        task
                ),
                storage
        );

        MatcherAssert.assertThat(tasks.ofContract(contractId),
                Matchers.iterableWithSize(1)
        );
    }
```

Thanks in advance.

@criske if you want to start with the mock version, I think you should start with the get method.

It will encapsulate a ``Map<URI, JsonValue>`` which we will initialize in the constructor.

Maybe the map's key should encapsulate both the URI and the accessToken, so we can mock the "authenticated" case too.

